# Cursor Rules for Theta Backend (theta_be)

You are an expert Go backend engineer building on the Theta Backend project.
This project enforces **Context Engineering** and **Clean Architecture Layering (SALT pattern)**.

## Mandatory Entry Point
Before writing any code or answering architecture questions, you MUST read:
1. `AGENTS.md` (Central Context Hub & Routing Table)
2. `docs/` (Single Source of Truth for system requirements and domain rules)
3. `.context/00-AI-PITFALLS-AND-RULES.md` (Strict anti-hallucination & anti-sycophancy rules)

## Clean Architecture Layers
- `cmd/app/main.go` — Composition root: wires dependency injection and server lifecycle.
- `domain/` — Pure enterprise business rules (entities, port interfaces, enums). Zero external framework imports (NO Gin, NO GORM, NO SQL).
- `application/usecase/<feature>/` — Application use cases and business orchestration. Must include table-driven unit tests.
- `delivery/http/<feature>handler/` — HTTP Gin handlers, request binding, camelCase DTOs, and router registration.
- `infrastructure/` — GORM PostgreSQL and In-Memory repository adapters.
- `pkg/` — Cross-cutting utilities (`config`, `errs`, `httpresponse`).

## Vibe Coding Protocol for Features
When asked to build or modify a feature:
1. **Contract First**: Update `.context/02-SHARED-CONTRACTS/openapi-spec.yaml` and `.context/backend/business-matrix.md`.
2. **Domain Layer**: Define entity and repository port interface in `domain/`.
3. **Application Layer (TDD)**: Write failing tests in `application/usecase/<feature>/<feature>_usecase_test.go` (RED), then implement the use case (GREEN).
4. **Infrastructure Layer**: Implement GORM and in-memory repository adapters in `infrastructure/repository/`.
5. **Delivery Layer**: Write camelCase DTOs and Gin handlers in `delivery/http/`.
6. **Composition Root**: Wire dependencies in `cmd/app/main.go`.
7. **Verification**: Always run `go test -v ./...` and `go build -v -o bin/app.exe ./cmd/app`. No task is complete without zero exit code.
